      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Gd(NO3)3·6H2O (5×10−5 mol) was added to a solution of triethanolamine (5×10−5 mol) in 0.01 L acetonitrile, then triethylamine (3×10−5 L) was added. The mixture was sealed in a 0.02 L glass vial, ultrasonicated for 30 min, heated at 343 K for 24 h, and slowly cooled to room temperature to give yellow block-shaped crystals.",
